	<section class="section">
		<h2>Who</h2>
		<p>I'm <strong>@qrak</strong>. Backend developer with AI/LLM experience; before that I worked with enterprise SAP environments at BSH Sprzęt Gospodarstwa Domowego. Semantic Signal is my own project, built after hours.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>The project</h2>
		<p>An open-source LLM trading agent: it reads candlestick charts as images, keeps semantic memory of closed trades, and applies deterministic risk limits before a decision is booked. Capital is simulated.</p>
		<p>The executor — the separate service that places orders — runs against an exchange testnet. That path stays on testnet until it has been verified, and the site says so.</p>
		<p>History: <a href="/story/">the full development history</a>. Numbers: <a href="/results/">the results page</a>.</p>
	</section>

